{
  "version": 1,
  "name": "Snapchat footage place-name ladder",
  "notes": [
    "Editable. Drives the narrow-to-wide place-name ladder for POST /api/scenes/:locationId/footage/snapchat (server/scene-footage/snapchat.js).",
    "The Snapchat plugin (plugin-1792945050, fetchSnapchatVideosByPlace) accepts ONLY place-name strings. It has no coordinate, radius or bbox input, so these entries translate a map coordinate into the names that are searched.",
    "level is one of landmark | neighborhood | district | city (narrow -> wide). parent links an entry to the next wider entry. radius_km is a planning radius around center used to decide which entry a coordinate falls in; it is NOT an official boundary.",
    "Centers marked source 'gazetteer' are copied from config/aoi/scene-aois.json or config/aoi/uae-interest.json; others are approximate operator-curated centers (OpenStreetMap-derived, rounded) and should be treated as approximate.",
    "names[0] is the display/matched name; every name in names is sent to the plugin in the same call for that level (aliases such as 'JBR')."
  ],
